{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/6dczuhkf","slide":5,"text":"All labelled arrows carry data. Process 4.5 uses greedy improvement and 2-opt / local search.","textPreview":"All labelled arrows carry data. Process 4.5 uses greedy improvement and 2-opt / local search.","textChars":93,"textLines":1,"bbox":[65,786,1470,46]}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/eiffqf","slide":5,"text":"Level 2 expands process 4. Receive Orders reads the validated order set. Retrieve Constraints adds capacity, driver availability, time windows and service times. Get Distances obtains a travel matrix from D6 and the Map API. Generate Initial Route constructs a feasible seed route where possible. Apply Optimization uses greedy improvement and 2-opt/local search to generate candidate routes. Check Constraints returns violation details for revision or sends a feasible plan to Calculate Metrics. Metrics include distance, estimated duration and a cost estimate based on supplied cost rules. Store Route writes D5 and the run outcome goes to D8. Infeasible orders remain explicit exceptions; the system must not silently break a hard constraint. A practical implementation needs a bounded search budget and a no-feasible-plan outcome. Map API requests and responses connect to 4.3 Get Distances. D6 supplies stored location data."}
{"kind":"slide","id":"sl/1ljva6","slide":6,"title":"Optimization & route recalculation","textShapes":17}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/wnip07y1","slide":6,"text":"Optimization & route recalculation","textPreview":"Optimization & route recalculation","textChars":34,"textLines":1,"bbox":[65,45,1470,64]}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/vm9872hg","slide":6,"text":"The objective is a lower-cost feasible plan, rather than a guarantee of the global optimum.","textPreview":"The objective is a lower-cost feasible plan, rather than a guarantee of the global optimum.","textChars":91,"textLines":1,"bbox":[65,116,1450,42]}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/a1g7yxgv","slide":6,"text":"RouteMind","textPreview":"RouteMind","textChars":9,"textLines":1,"bbox":[65,849,400,22]}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/907q5sza","slide":6,"text":"06","textPreview":"06","textChars":2,"textLines":1,"bbox":[1465,845,70,28]}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/8zypwnyp","slide":6,"text":"How the planner improves a route","textPreview":"How the planner improves a route","textChars":32,"textLines":1,"bbox":[65,213,820,45]}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/nyp83ihk","slide":6,"text":"1  Build a starting plan","textPreview":"1  Build a starting plan","textChars":24,"textLines":1,"bbox":[65,301,835,41]}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/mxg7udgz","slide":6,"text":"Choose feasible next stops using travel time,\npriority, remaining capacity and delivery windows.","textPreview":"Choose feasible next stops using travel time, | priority, remaining capacity and delivery windows.","textChars":96,"textLines":2,"bbox":[65,350,835,79]}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/lw7q18ze","slide":6,"text":"2  Improve the stop sequence","textPreview":"2  Improve the stop sequence","textChars":28,"textLines":1,"bbox":[65,441,835,41]}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/0vypsnyt","slide":6,"text":"Use 2-opt to reverse a route segment when it\nreduces cost and keeps all constraints satisfied.","textPreview":"Use 2-opt to reverse a route segment when it | reduces cost and keeps all constraints satisfied.","textChars":94,"textLines":2,"bbox":[65,490,835,79]}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/ih8zulon","slide":6,"text":"3  Compare and keep the better plan","textPreview":"3  Compare and keep the better plan","textChars":35,"textLines":1,"bbox":[65,581,835,41]}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/3ihg3q58","slide":6,"text":"Check total distance, estimated duration and\nunassigned orders before saving the result.","textPreview":"Check total distance, estimated duration and | unassigned orders before saving the result.","textChars":88,"textLines":2,"bbox":[65,630,835,79]}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/43qhwv6d","slide":6,"text":"When delivery plans change","textPreview":"When delivery plans change","textChars":26,"textLines":1,"bbox":[987,213,545,45]}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/54zy5gny","slide":6,"text":"New or cancelled order\nDriver delay\nUpdated customer availability","textPreview":"New or cancelled order | Driver delay | Updated customer availability","textChars":65,"textLines":3,"bbox":[987,301,540,122]}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/ud8zq1ob","slide":6,"text":"Replanning rule","textPreview":"Replanning rule","textChars":15,"textLines":1,"bbox":[987,474,540,39]}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/vehgz65w","slide":6,"text":"Keep completed stops fixed. Recalculate\nremaining deliveries from each driver’s\ncurrent location and remaining capacity.","textPreview":"Keep completed stops fixed. Recalculate | remaining deliveries from each driver’s | current location and remaining capacity.","textChars":120,"textLines":3,"bbox":[987,530,535,135]}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/gfqhsb6h","slide":6,"text":"Publish the revised route and ETA\nto the affected driver and customer.","textPreview":"Publish the revised route and ETA | to the affected driver and customer.","textChars":70,"textLines":2,"bbox":[987,702,535,77]}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/hgzy1gn2","slide":6,"text":"Hard limits: capacity and required time windows. Priority influences the choice among feasible plans.","textPreview":"Hard limits: capacity and required time windows. Priority influences the choice among feasible plans.","textChars":101,"textLines":1,"bbox":[65,786,1470,46]}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/1ljva6","slide":6,"text":"A greedy rule makes a locally useful choice while constructing or improving a plan. It does not prove global optimality. A 2-opt move cuts two edges and reverses the intermediate sequence; the system accepts the change only if the route remains feasible and improves the objective. With multiple vehicles, initial allocation chooses feasible vehicle assignments and local search can also relocate orders between vehicles. Time windows require arrival-time and service-time checks. Replanning preserves completed deliveries and accounts for current location, remaining load and driver availability. Metrics are estimated, not promised savings."}
